<title>ABU DHABI: UAE central bank urges money laundering checks.</title>
<headline>UAE central bank urges money laundering checks.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates Central Bank on Tuesday urged financial institutions in the Gulf state to ensure that they are not part of money laundering schemes.</p>
<p>&quot;All financial institutions operating in the UAE are expected to protect the UAE financial system from being used to facilitate illicit activities,&quot; Central Bank Governor Sultan bin Nasser al-Suweidi said in a speech to a finance conference.</p>
<p>&quot;Grounded in the concept of 'knowing your customer' each institution will, in the near future, be expected to adopt internal control policies, procedures and compliance measures best suited to protect its own operations,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
